# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js (App Router) project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Component Configuration
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, following the official Vercel documentation guidelines for Next.js App Router

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics Quickstart documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I:

1. **Identified the framework**: Confirmed this is a Next.js project using the App Router (based on the presence of `app/layout.tsx`)
2. **Used the correct package manager**: npm (detected from `package-lock.json`)
3. **Applied framework-specific instructions**: Used the Next.js App Router setup, importing from `@vercel/analytics/next` and placing the component in the root layout
4. **Preserved existing code structure**: The Analytics component was added without modifying any existing functionality (ClerkProvider, fonts, styling, etc.)

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linter passed with no issues
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ All existing functionality preserved

## Next Steps

To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy this application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics tab in your Vercel project dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button
4. Analytics data will begin tracking automatically after deployment

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
